cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "PJM and MISO Cold-Spell Calibration Benchmark: When Cold-Spell Calibration Fails to Transfer"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-22
authors:
  - family-names: Goehner
    given-names: Dresden
    email: dresdengoehner@outlook.com
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Jurupa Valley, CA, USA"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DresdenGman/PJM-Cold-Calibration-Benchmark"
abstract: >-
  Code, frozen protocol, derived data and full results for a benchmark of
  probabilistic load forecasting in extreme cold: four PJM events (2014 polar
  vortex, 2015 anchor, 2017-18 cold snap, 2022 Winter Storm Elliott) and a
  pre-specified replication on MISO (2017-18, 2019, 2022). Three forecasters
  and five conformal calibrators are evaluated at day-ahead and one-hour
  horizons under strictly chronological evaluation and under retrospective
  leave-one-event-out transfer. Version 1.1.0 adds the MISO replication, a
  forecast-temperature sensitivity arm and the prior-winter calibration
  sensitivity.
keywords:
  - probabilistic load forecasting
  - conformal prediction
  - calibration transfer
  - extreme cold events
  - PJM
  - MISO
  - forecast evaluation
